# The optional FFmpeg audio decoder (org.jellyfin.media3:media3-ffmpeg-decoder) lives in the package
# androidx.media3.decoder.ffmpeg, which is inside the R8 package scope. SoftAudio.kt and Media3's
# DefaultRenderersFactory load FfmpegAudioRenderer by reflection, and the native library calls back into
# the decoder classes by name. Keep the whole (small) package unchanged.
-keep class androidx.media3.decoder.ffmpeg.** { *; }

# The app's own code stays exactly as written (T-024): R8 does not remove, rename or optimize anything in
# com.ipvio.**. R8 runs over the whole app; this rule limits its work to the libraries.
-keep class com.ipvio.** { *; }

# No renaming and no repackaging (T-024). With AGP 9.x and the library-only package scope, R8 moved renamed
# subclasses of kotlin.text into another package, which made a package-private superclass inaccessible
# (app crashed at start: IllegalAccessError in androidx.startup.InitializationProvider). -dontobfuscate alone
# was not enough then: since AGP 9.1 R8 moves classes into one package by default, and -dontrepackage is the
# documented switch against that. Optimization of the libraries (inlining, removing unused code) stays on.
-dontobfuscate
-dontrepackage
